# Service-managed: this file is installed into /run/udev/rules.d/ only
# while trackpad-guard.service is running, and removed when it stops.
# See trackpad-guard/scripts/manage-udev-rule.sh.
#
# Why: when trackpad-guard is running, the daemon EVIOCGRAB's the real
# AMIRA touchpad and exposes a virtual uinput device to libinput. We
# need libinput to skip the real device or it'd fight us for events.
# But when trackpad-guard is *not* running there's no virtual
# replacement, so leaving this rule installed would mean the login
# screen / a user who toggled the daemon off has no touchpad at all.
# Hence the service-managed lifecycle.
#
# It lives in /run (tmpfs), NOT /etc: a clean stop removes it via
# ExecStopPost, but a power loss / panic never runs ExecStopPost. A
# persistent copy would then orphan into the next boot and strand the
# user with no pointer. In /run it is wiped every boot, so an unclean
# death degrades to "real touchpad works" rather than "no touchpad".

# The AMIRA's mouse-class interface gets named "Mouse" under hid-generic
# and "Touchpad" under hid-multitouch — catch both.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="AMIRA-KEYBOAR USB KEYBOARD Mouse", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="AMIRA-KEYBOAR USB KEYBOARD Touchpad", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
